      "text": [
        "2487 - وَ نَهَى رَسُولُ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ : أَنْ يُتَخَطَّى اَلْقِطَارُ قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ وَ لِمَ قَالَ «لِأَنَّهُ لَيْسَ مِنْ قِطَارٍ إِلاَّ وَ مَا بَيْنَ اَلْبَعِيرِ إِلَى اَلْبَعِيرِ شَيْطَانٌ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2487 - The Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace and blessings of Allah (swt) be upon him and his family) forbade stepping over the camel line (caravan).\nIt was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah (swt), why?\"\nProphet (sw) replied: \"Because there is not a single camel line except that between one camel and the next there is a devil.\""
        ]
      }
